Alembic migrations — single-database configuration.

Baseline: 0001_initial_baseline.py creates all 5 tables (anchors, live_sessions,
danmakus, script_segments, pipeline_steps) plus the audit-added indexes.

Two deployment scenarios:

1) Fresh database (new staging/prod):
     cd backend
     alembic upgrade head

2) Existing dev database (tables already created by main.py's create_all but
   without the new indexes):
     cd backend
     # Mark schema as baselined without re-creating tables:
     alembic stamp 0001_baseline
     # Indexes will be auto-added by main.py's Base.metadata.create_all on next
     # startup (create_all is additive). Or to be explicit, drop the dev DB and
     # use path (1).

For new schema changes:
     alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe_change"
     # Review the generated file before committing — autogenerate is best-effort.
     alembic upgrade head

The env.py reads DATABASE_URL from app/config.py (single source of truth) and
strips the +asyncpg dialect tag, so you don't need to maintain a separate sync
URL in alembic.ini.
